{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"fb1d0e558f4641c7850fe8aaca4068df\\\",\\\"B6-commit-install\\\",\\\"B16-client-reply\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S20-exec\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"An attempt to extend the owner-alive re-proposal protection to the client's actual reply (commit of the re-proposed instance, execution, and bytes written to the client writer) ran into a construction obstacle worth recording rather than hiding: the harness that drives that scenario is the simpler one, which has no peer-message delivery helper, so the re-proposed instance's PreAccept reply would have to be prepared by hand instead of produced by a peer's handler - exactly the substitution the protocol findings have been careful to avoid. The mechanism itself remains confirmed (claim C5: the operation is put back on the propose channel), and the reply path is unchanged: execution applies the committed commands and answers the client when the proposal is still attached, so the missing piece is only an end-to-end observation, not an unexplained mechanism.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"an end-to-end client-reply observation after a NOOP recovery, which needs a harness that both drives the re-proposal and delivers peer messages through the real codec (the machinery exists in the recovery harnesses and could be combined)\\\",\n   \\\"the reader-side reaction to a displaced stream, which cannot be exercised in-package\\\",\n   \\\"the two paused candidates' resume conditions, the attribution issue on the superseded C1 artifact, and the interpretation question for the inert transitive-conflict branch\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Recording the obstacle prevents a future attempt from producing a weaker witness by preparing the peer reply, and it states precisely what the remaining observation needs. No requirement, premise or earlier result changes.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Records a construction obstacle found while trying to extend the client-completion protection to an end-to-end reply observation, so a later attempt builds it with message delivery rather than a prepared reply. No map object changes.\\\",\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-client-reply-note.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-client-reply-note.json 2>&1 | head -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
